This licence covers the PAPERS of this series. Paths are relative to docs/papers/, one directory
up from this file:

  p1-conditional-lever/main.tex     p1-conditional-lever/figures/
  p2-repair-not-detection/main.tex  p2-repair-not-detection/figures/
  p3-silent-no-op/main.tex          p3-silent-no-op/figures/
  shared/preamble.tex               shared/loop.tex
  shared/series.tex                 shared/references.bib
  shared/figures/                   README.md
  SUBMISSION.md                     REPRODUCE.md

and any PDF built from them.

Paths are given relative to docs/papers/ because this file no longer sits beside the papers. It was
written when the series was one paper in one directory and it said "the PAPER in this directory",
naming main.tex, SUBMISSION.md and REPRODUCE.md. The split into three moved this file into shared/,
where none of those three exist, so the grant named a layout that had stopped existing. Copyright
and permission are unchanged; what changed is that the scope now resolves.

It does NOT cover the software in this repository. Code is licensed Apache-2.0; see the LICENSE
file at the repository root. The two are separate grants deliberately: the code carries a patent
grant and a NOTICE requirement that make no sense for a document, and the paper carries a
redistribution and derivative-works permission that Apache-2.0 expresses differently.

  Copyright (c) 2026 Vladimir Rotariu

  You are free to share (copy and redistribute in any medium or format) and adapt (remix,
  transform, and build upon) this material for any purpose, including commercially, provided you
  give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate if changes were made.

  Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
  Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This is the same licence selected for the arXiv submission (see SUBMISSION.md). arXiv's own default,
the Perpetual Non-Exclusive Licence, was declined: it grants arXiv distribution rights while
limiting re-use by everyone else, which would contradict a paper whose contribution is a reporting
practice plus an artifact that other people are asked to re-run. The arXiv licence choice is
irrevocable once a version is announced.
